 construction: it modifies the noun 'susceptibility gene' and refers to the gene's role, so it is annotated as a Modifier and not as a Composite Mention or Specific Disease.\",\"guideline_section\":\"What to Annotate §3: Annotate disease mentions that are used as Modifiers for other concepts\"}]}", "type": "text"}], "diagnostics": null, "model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "role": "assistant", "stop_details": null, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "stop_sequence": null, "type": "message", "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 4103, "output_tokens": 1311, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 978}, "service_tier": "batch", "speed": "standard"}}}